---
import LegalLayout from '@/components/legal/LegalLayout.astro';
import DecisionNote from '@/components/legal/DecisionNote.astro';
import { packages } from '@/data/packages';
import { approvedServices } from '@/data/services';
import { site } from '@/data/site';

const naira = (n: number) => `₦${n.toLocaleString('en-NG')}`;
const sections = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'What these terms cover' },
  { id: 'services', label: 'Services' },
  { id: 'proposals', label: 'Proposals and approvals' },
  { id: 'prices', label: 'Prices and payment' },
  { id: 'revisions', label: 'Revisions and changes' },
  { id: 'ip', label: 'Ownership and content' },
  { id: 'support', label: 'Support after launch' },
  { id: 'concepts', label: 'Studio concepts' },
  { id: 'liability', label: 'Liability, law and disputes' },
];
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of service"
  heading="Terms of service"
  description="Draft terms of service for SabiForge Digital, for owner and legal review. Not an approved document."
  document="terms"
  sections={sections}
>
  <h2 id="scope">1. What these terms cover</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are intended to cover the use of the {site.name} website and projects the studio
    carries out for clients. Each project is also governed by a written proposal.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="T1" />

  <h2 id="services">2. Services</h2>
  <p>The website currently describes these services:</p>
  <ul>
    {approvedServices.map((s) => (
      <li>{s.name}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>
    Whether the studio takes on a project is decided after a first conversation. The studio will
    tell you if it believes you do not need its services.
  </p>

  <h2 id="proposals">3. Proposals and approvals</h2>
  <p>
    The website describes this order of work. Each project follows it unless the proposal says
    otherwise:
  </p>
  <ol class="list-decimal pl-6">
    <li>A first conversation and recommendation.</li>
    <li>
      A written proposal stating scope, content responsibilities, timeline, price and third-party
      costs. It is approved before design begins.
    </li>
    <li>Designs are approved before development begins.</li>
    <li>A private staging site is reviewed before launch.</li>
    <li>Launch is approved by the client, followed by a handover.</li>
  </ol>
  <DecisionNote id="T13" />

  <h2 id="prices">4. Prices and payment</h2>
  <p>These are the approved package prices as shown on the website, in Nigerian naira:</p>
  <ul>
    {packages.map((p) => (
      <li>
        <strong>{p.name}:</strong> {p.id === 'ecommerce' ? 'from ' : ''}
        {p.price === null ? 'a custom amount' : naira(p.price)} for {p.scope.toLowerCase()}.
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>
    Third-party costs, such as domains, hosting, platform subscriptions, paid themes and apps,
    payment-gateway fees and licensed images or fonts, are quoted separately. Custom scopes for a
    service are quoted individually.
  </p>
  <p>
    A founding-client rate of 10% is shown for the Launch, Business and Online Catalog packages. It
    does not apply to Full E-commerce. The number of founding places has not been decided.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="T12" />
  <DecisionNote id="T2" />
  <DecisionNote id="T8" />

  <h2 id="revisions">5. Revisions and changes</h2>
  <p>
    The website says revision rounds and timelines are written into each proposal. No number of
    rounds has been approved for any package.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="T3" />
  <DecisionNote id="T4" />

  <h2 id="ip">6. Ownership and content</h2>
  <p>
    Ownership of the finished website, licences for third-party materials, and the studio’s right to
    show completed work have not been decided.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="T5" />
  <DecisionNote id="T6" />
  <DecisionNote id="T11" />

  <h2 id="support">7. Support after launch</h2>
  <p>
    The website says ongoing care is optional and defined per agreement. No post-launch fix period,
    response time or care-plan price has been approved.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="T7" />

  <h2 id="concepts">8. Studio concepts</h2>
  <p>
    The brands shown on the Work page (Àdùn Table, Kòrà Home, Mend Physio Studio and Tallyhouse) are
    fictional concepts created by the studio. They are not client projects, and the prices, people,
    invoices and health wording in them are invented for illustration.
  </p>

  <h2 id="liability">9. Liability, law and disputes</h2>
  <p>
    The studio makes no promise on this website about traffic, search rankings, sales or other
    business results, which depend on many factors beyond a website. Binding wording on liability
    and the governing law has not been drafted.
  </p>
  <DecisionNote id="T9" />
  <DecisionNote id="T10" />
</LegalLayout>
